cards.question:
```
Translate these shorthand operators into the longer if statements they represent.
string city = person?.Address?.City ?? "Athens";
Assume:
class Person
{
  public Address? Address { get; set; }
}

class Address
  public string? City {get; set; }
}

cards.answer:
```
string city;
if (person  == null)
{
  city = "Athens";
}
else if (person.Address == null)
{
    city = "Athens";
}
else if (person.Address.City == null)
{
    city = "Athens";
}
else
{
    city = person.Address.City;
}


Cleaner version:
string city = "Athens";
if (person != null &&
    person.Address != null &&
    person.Address.City != null)
{
   city = person.Address.City;
}
